eration keeps the result inside $\\mathbb{R}^3$ under the vector-space structure?","options":["Adding $(1,0,2)$ and $(0,3)$ to get $(1,3,2)$","Deleting one coordinate from $(1,0,2)$","Adding $(1,0,2)$ and $(0,3,-1)$ to get $(1,3,1)$","Sorting $(1,0,2)$ to get $(0,1,2)$ as the required operation"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3e09c83b2c2c463e0ef50a99"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_coordinate_space_844bb0b9_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is an element of $\\mathbb{R}^n$?","options":["An unordered set of $n$ real numbers","A single complex number only","A finite cover of $\\mathbb{R}$","An ordered $n$-tuple of real numbers"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"55325caa971356b762b0222c"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_coordinate_space_844bb0b9_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does the dimension $n$ specify in $\\mathbb{R}^n$?","options":["The number of open covers","The number of real coordinates in each point","The number of possible metrics, in every case without exception.","The largest coordinate value"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"07da4e5723825f4acc727a05"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_coordinate_space_844bb0b9_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What algebraic structure does $\\mathbb{R}^n$ get from component-wise operations?","options":["A real vector space","A topology only","An open cover","A single vector"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d4878f1d470b17c0b325684"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_coordinate_space_844bb0b9_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which object belongs to $\\mathbb{R}^3$?","options":["$(1,0)$","$\\{1,0,-2\\}$","$(1,0,-2)$","$1+2\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1f5eff80186054c99e423638"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_coordinate_space_844bb0b9_017","difficulty":"basic","qu